    "summary": "High‑energy ’71 set with smoking Smokestack Lightning and stellar Brokedown Palace",
    "blurb": "A crisp soundboard capture that showcases the Dead’s classic 1971 repertoire. Highlights include a searing Smokestack Lightning, a soaring solo on Brokedown Palace and tight, driving rhythm on Not Fade Away. Overall performance is high‑energy and tightly sequenced.",
    "review": "December 7, 1971 at New York's Felt Forum finds the Grateful Dead in peak form, delivering a set that crackles with electric intensity. The Miller soundboard tape captures Jerry’s beautiful, loud tone—especially his soul‑melting solo on Brokedown Palace—while Phil’s melodic bass bombs through each groove, anchoring the band’s high‑energy push. Pigpen’s harmonica and vocal bursts add a bluesy edge, and Keith’s piano textures weave nicely into the mix. Standout moments abound: a scorching Smokestack Lightning that rides the room’s excitement, a tight Not Fade Away/Feel Good jam in the second set, and an uplifting One More Saturday Night encore that caps a night of classic ’71 material.",
